# What never goes into the build context.
#
# Two reasons for every line here: the image should be small, and it must not
# contain a secret. The second one is the one that matters. An image is cached,
# copied and pushed to a registry, and anything COPY . . picks up is in it.

# Secrets. The real .env stays on the machine it was written on.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.docker.example

# Rebuilt inside the image; copying them in would only be stale and large.
node_modules
.next
out

# Version control and CI.
.git
.github

# Test output, screenshots and local logs.
test-results
playwright-report
snapshots
*.log
coverage

# Local-only notes.
CLAUDE.md
session.md

# Runtime state on the server, which the app never reads from the image.
# Uploads belong in the volume; a local ./uploads baked in would be shadowed by
# it anyway, and could carry a developer's test images into production.
backups
uploads

# A local copy of the country database. The image fetches its own.
geo
